distinguish unaudited from reviewed-but-not-approved. Keep this snapshot in the report
so later edits to the working target cannot erase what was reviewed.

## Result
Important findings, corrections, rebuttals, and outstanding issues.

## Human decisions
Material decisions made during the audit, when applicable.
For a question override: exact instruction, identified version, actual review
outcome, unresolved concerns, and any report-publication error. Otherwise: none.

## Next step
The human review or other decision now needed.
\`\`\`

## Host dispatch: OpenCode

Identify the current writer's provider and model from the Provider ID and Model ID
in the \`# Your Model\` context.

Check model availability using \`opencode.models\`, discovering that native tool
through Code Mode if needed.

Start a foreground native \`subagent\` call with \`agent: "explore"\`,
explicit \`model\`, a short \`description\`, and the filled auditor assignment as
\`prompt\`. Omit \`sessionID\` initially. Keep the returned \`sessionID\`. Each follow-up passes
the same agent, model, and \`sessionID\`. Follow native output references and pages
when reading results.

\`explore\` cannot load skills, edit files, or launch subagents; its shell remains
available, so read-only is still an instruction.

### Question presentation

The native \`question\` tool accepts a \`questions\` array. Consult its active schema
for every authored field: question text, header, ordered option labels and
descriptions, and \`multiple\`. OpenCode automatically provides a free-form answer;
do not add a duplicate free-form option. Include that answer mechanism in review
context. Each question in an array is a separate audit target; check all included
versions before sending the call. Prose choices need the same complete presentation
review, including surrounding explanation and recommendation.

## Configuration

    {
      "reviewers": {
        "gateway/team/writer": "other/reviewer#high"
      },
      "maxRounds": 3,
      "artifactDirectory": "../audit-notes"
    }

## Registry content integration

- brainstorming: integrated
- writing-plans: unavailable — "Source skill missing"

This is not a per-agent permission verdict. Report known native load denials without enumerating unknown permissions or enabling skills. For unavailable integrations, check that this plugin is listed after Superpowers and that the source skill is present. Manual auditing requires its command and this shared skill to be registered and permitted.
